# Per-element callee with multiple outputs — one FunctionDef per read field

Multi-output (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3a, 2026-08-25): a per-element callee that
declares more than one output lowers ONE FunctionDef per read output FIELD,
named `<callee> <field>`. `KamerMulti` declares two outputs; the caller reads
only `.bedrag` in the map body, so exactly `KamerMulti bedrag` is synthesised
(`grondslag + 100`) and the map folds to a scalar — the direct-map-body sibling
of the tutorial's fused multi-output. Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope KamerMulti:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer
  output korting content integer

scope KamerMulti:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag + 100
  definition korting equals grondslag + 5

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  output totaal content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition totaal equals
    combine all b
      among (map each g among grondslagen to (output of KamerMulti with { -- grondslag: g }).bedrag)
      in acc initially 0 with (acc + b)
```
